{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TensorEmbedding","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TensorTraceCharacter"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace.trace_braidAt_one_eq_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace.trace_braidAt_one_eq_card","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidingTrace.lean#L146-L152","doc":"Consistency: at `q = qi = 1` the general-`q` sum counts the states fixed by the\ntransposition, and agrees with `trace_braidAt_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace.trace_braidAt_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace.trace_braidAt_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidingTrace.lean#L129-L144","doc":"**The braiding's trace as an explicit sum over basis states.**\n\nThe diagonal entry at `a` depends only on the two site values: `q` when `a i = a j` (the\nsymmetric channel), `q − qi` when `a i < a j`, and `0` when `a i > a j` — the asymmetry\nbeing the ordering built into Jimbo's `Ř`.\n\nLeft as a sum rather than a closed form deliberately: collapsing it to `2^{n−2}(3q − qi)`\nneeds the state count `#{a | (a i, a j) = (x, y)} = 2^{n−2}`, a separate lemma that also\ndrags `ℕ`-subtraction into the exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace.trace_braidAt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace.trace_braidAt_one","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidingTrace.lean#L115-L125","doc":"**The classical character, from the braiding.** At `q = 1` the trace of the braiding at\nsites `i ≠ j` is `2^{orbitCount (i j)}` — the `2^{c(σ)}` of `ClassicalTraceFloor`, obtained\nfrom `Ř` rather than assumed alongside it.\n\nNo new computation: this is `TensorTraceCharacter.trace_permMatrixOf_indexPerm` read through\nthe identification above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace.braidAt_one_eq_permMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace.braidAt_one_eq_permMatrix","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidingTrace.lean#L93-L113","doc":"**At `q = 1` the braiding IS the transposition's permutation matrix.**\n\nNot \"degenerates to something flip-like\" — literally the matrix\n`permMatrixOf (indexPerm (swap i j) (Fin 2))` whose trace `TensorTraceCharacter` computes.\nThis is the joint between the braiding half of quantum Schur–Weyl and the character half.\n\nNo `i ≠ j` hypothesis is needed, and the degenerate case is not vacuous: at `i = j` both\nsides are the identity matrix — `swap i i = 1`, and the braiding's condition collapses to\n`a = b` — so the trace below reads `2^{orbitCount 1} = 2^n`, the dimension of `V^{⊗n}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace.swap_indexPerm_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.BraidingTrace.swap_indexPerm_iff","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/BraidingTrace.lean#L65-L91","doc":"The braiding's matrix condition and the transposition's are the same condition.\n\n`Ř` at `q = 1` sends `a ↦ b` with weight `1` exactly when `a` and `b` agree away from the\ntwo sites and are swapped on them — which is precisely `b ∘ (i j) = a`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}